        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "In Utah, the best time to replace a roof is late spring through early fall (May to October). These months offer mild temperatures and dry conditions, allowing sealants on asphalt shingles to cure properly without freezing or extreme heat.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "The ideal season for your project depends on your exact goals:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Best Weather: Fall is widely considered the peak season. Temperatures average a comfortable 65\u00b0 F to 70\u00b0 F, and there is generally less unpredictable rain.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              5,
              6
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Fastest Scheduling: Late spring and early summer. You will avoid the high-demand \"storm rush\" that happens right before the heavy Utah snows.",
            "reference_indexes": [
              7
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Best Price: Late winter to early spring (February/March). This is a \"shoulder season\" where local contractors are eager to secure jobs before the busy season hits, making it easier to negotiate competitive bids."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you're planning a replacement, let me know:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "What city or county\nyou live in"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The approximate size of your roof"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "The material you are looking to install (e.g., asphalt, metal)"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can connect you with local contractors or help you estimate a more accurate timeline."
      }
